Verify that a CDB2_MASTER handle connects to the master when the database's
hosts come with cluster type "configured", as a proxy such as prox2 supplies
them on CDB2_BEFORE_DISCOVERY. CDB2_MASTER handles skip the "configured"
shortcut in get_connection_int(), and cdb2_get_dbhosts() used to discard the
supplied hosts and ask comdb2db for a "configured" cluster. A plain handle is
the control, along with the suite's own config and a config that lists the
hosts under the "configured" tier.
